    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><strong>Dream Rite.</strong> You learn a formalized way to question the Great Work itself.</p><p><strong>Once per Soma Break</strong>, after at least 10 minutes of quiet trance or sleep, you may perform a Dream Rite. Choose one mode when you begin the rite:</p><ul><li><strong>Route Rite (Travel):</strong> You focus on a planned route or upcoming travel leg. The Dream shows you an omen about its dangers or opportunities. You reroll the lowest die on the next hazard-avoidance roll for that route, or your GM may allow you to ignore the first minor hazard triggered on that route.</li><li><strong>Hex Rite (World-State):</strong> You focus on a single hex. The Dream reveals its Sephirotic/Qliphothic tilt and one major unseen factor. You gain a +2 bonus on the next roll or OP test to influence that hex (such as shifting alignment, stabilizing, exploiting, or cleansing).</li><li><strong>Faction Rite (Intent):</strong> You focus on a faction or key NPC. The Dream shows you their immediate agenda and symbolic trajectory. You gain a +2 bonus on the next social, intrigue, or Soft Power OP action targeting that faction or NPC.</li><li><strong>Spark Rite (Metaphysics):</strong> You focus on a known Spark, relic, or metaphysical event. The Dream offers guidance or warning. You gain a +1d4 bonus on the next roll directly related to handling that Spark or object, and the GM may soften the first minor mishap if your approach fits the omen.</li></ul><p>The Dream never lies, but its answers are often symbolic, incomplete, or framed in imagery. Mechanical bonuses apply to one relevant roll or test as agreed at the table.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
